  "findings": [
    "15-case d matrix preserves result sets on both backends. Existing pending-only unique index already serves pending decisions.",
    "Extended e PostgreSQL passes. Turso e/f/j fail result equality on large-agent decision history.",
    "j samples show baseline returning older rows 6690..6709 while added index returns expected 16..35.",
    "64-row h and 8192-row narrow i controls pass. 8192-row wide k fails known expected oracle on no-index and forced-scan paths, but both ascending/descending indexes return expected rows. Sorter root cause not established.",
    "PostgreSQL future-heavy due scan uses BitmapOr with status/next; third created column unnecessary in g. No final production index selection or migration yet."
  ]
